---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Reading the Law handles information when you visit the website, including what's collected automatically and what happens if you join the matchmaking waitlist."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" subtitle="Last updated August 2026" />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <Callout tone="info" title="Plain-language summary">
      We don't run accounts, ads, or trackers on this Site, and we don't collect anything through a form of
      our own. Visiting the Site generates the same kind of basic technical logs any website generates.
      Loading our fonts pings Google's font service. If you join the matchmaking waitlist, you're filling
      out a Google Form, so that information is handled under Google's privacy policy, not just ours. The
      full policy below spells this out in more detail.
    </Callout>

    <article class="prose-legal">
      <h2>1. Who this policy covers</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Reading the Law ("we," "us," or "our") handles information in
        connection with the website at readingthelaw.org (the "Site"). It doesn't cover any third-party
        site or service we link to, including the Google Form we currently use for our matchmaking waitlist;
        those are covered by the relevant third party's own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information we collect automatically</h2>
      <p>
        Like most websites, our hosting provider automatically logs some technical information whenever you
        visit, such as your IP address, browser and device type, pages viewed, referring page, and
        timestamps. This information is collected through standard server and hosting logs rather than
        through any tracking script we've added ourselves, and we use it only in aggregate, for purposes
        like keeping the Site secure and understanding overall traffic patterns.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        We don't set our own cookies or use third-party advertising or analytics trackers on the Site. Our
        hosting provider may use minimal technical cookies necessary to serve the Site reliably. If that
        changes (for example, if we add analytics in the future), we'll update this policy to describe what
        we've added and why.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third-party services used by this Site</h2>
      <p>We rely on a small number of third-party services to run the Site:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hosting (Vercel).</strong> The Site is hosted on Vercel's infrastructure, which processes standard connection and request data to serve pages to you.</li>
        <li><strong>Fonts (Google Fonts).</strong> We load typefaces from Google's font service. Loading a page on this Site may send your IP address and browser information to Google as part of that request. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a> for details.</li>
        <li><strong>Matchmaking waitlist (Google Forms).</strong> The "Join the Waitlist" link on our <a href="/matchmaking/">matchmaking page</a> currently opens a Google Form in a new tab. Any name, email address, or other information you submit there is collected and stored by Google on our behalf, subject to <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and, where applicable, Google Forms' terms. We use that information solely to follow up about the matchmaking platform.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Information you send us directly</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us at <a href="mailto:readingthelaw@gmail.com">readingthelaw@gmail.com</a>, we'll have
        access to your email address and whatever you choose to include in that message. We use it only to
        respond to you and don't add it to any mailing list without your separate consent.
      </p>

      <h2>6. How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use the limited information described above to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Operate, maintain, and secure the Site.</li>
        <li>Understand overall usage patterns so we can improve the content.</li>
        <li>Respond to emails you send us.</li>
        <li>Follow up with people who join the matchmaking waitlist once that platform is ready.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. How we share information</h2>
      <p>
        We don't sell personal information, and we don't share it with third parties for their own
        marketing purposes. We may share information with the service providers described above (our
        hosting provider, Google) to the extent necessary for them to provide their service to us, or if
        required to do so by law, subpoena, or other legal process.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Standard hosting logs are retained only as long as our hosting provider's default retention period.
        Waitlist submissions are retained in the connected Google Form or spreadsheet until the matchmaking
        platform launches or until we no longer need them for that purpose, whichever comes first. Emails
        you send us are retained as long as reasonably necessary to address your inquiry.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can decline to submit the waitlist form or email us; doing so just means we won't have any way
        to follow up with you. Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights over information
        held about you, such as the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of information
        you've submitted to us directly. To make such a request regarding information you've sent us by
        email, contact <a href="mailto:readingthelaw@gmail.com">readingthelaw@gmail.com</a>. For information
        submitted through the Google Form, you'll generally need to contact Google directly or use the
        controls Google provides.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Site isn't directed at children, and we don't knowingly collect personal information from
        anyone under 13. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, contact us and
        we'll take appropriate steps to remove it.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on our hosting provider's standard security practices to protect the Site. No method of
        transmission over the internet or electronic storage is completely secure, so we can't guarantee
        absolute security for any information transmitted to or through the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page
        reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be reflected on this page; we encourage you
        to review it periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy, or requests regarding your information, can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:readingthelaw@gmail.com">readingthelaw@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
